WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.690
The demand for greater Asian representation
in Hollywood has never been higher than it

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:05.690
is today.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.580
Luckily, with Shang-Chi and the Legend of
the Ten Rings, Marvel seems to be putting

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.390
their money where their mouth is.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.860
Here's what you need to know before you see
Shang-Chi.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.600
Like every other project in Marvel's Phase
4, Shang-Chi has taken a long and bumpy road

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.880
to movie theaters.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.000
The film was initially set to kick off on
February 12th, 2021, making it the third theatrical

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.390
release for the Phase 4 lineup, after Black
Widow and Eternals.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:34.930
That was announced all the way back in 2019,
however, when nobody had any idea what the

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.120
future held.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.760
Obviously, 2020's COVID-19 pandemic turned
the world upside down, and basically every

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.039
studio in Hollywood ground to a halt, including
Marvel.

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:49.670
Both WandaVision and The Falcon and the Winter
Soldier hit Disney+ before their feature-length

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.690
cousins could return to theaters.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:56.199
And then, after a whole lot of reshuffling,
Shang-Chi battled its way to the #2 spot on

00:00:56.199 --> 00:01:00.369
the new theatrical release calendar, sliding
in between Black Widow and Eternals.

00:01:00.369 --> 00:01:05.490
As it stands, The Legend of the Ten Rings
is expected to hit theaters on September 3rd,

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.490
2021.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:12.460
Marvel has apparently heard the longtime cry
for diversification of not only cast but crew

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:18.710
as well, as the studio has chosen Asian-American
filmmaker Destin Daniel Cretton to helm Shang-Chi.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:23.360
He joins Eternals director Chloe Zhao as the
first filmmakers of Asian descent to join

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.160
the MCU in Phase 4.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:30.770
Cretton's standout project so far is the 2013
film Short Term 12, a story about troubled

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.170
teenagers and their carers living together
in a group home.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:39.220
Much of Shang-Chi's comics history is checkered,
to say the least, featuring a number of racist

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.470
"Oriental mysticism" tropes and "Yellow Peril"
villains.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:46.640
Bringing on talent of actual Asian heritage
is a positive sign that Marvel Studios is

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.409
interested in reflecting the real world more
accurately.

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:54.250
Casting Asian actors is all well and good,
of course — but placing the movie's creative

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:58.490
vision in the hands of a director of Asian
descent is an even better way of avoiding

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:01.659
the mistakes made by the earliest Shang-Chi
comics.

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:09.200
Chinese-Canadian actor Simu Liu was introduced
at Marvel's SDCC 2019 panel as Shang-Chi less

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.170
than a week after getting cast.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:15.870
He was born in Harbin, China, and immigrated
to a suburb in Toronto, when he was 5 years

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:16.870
old.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:21.219
Liu is best known for his role as the former
delinquent son Jung in Kim's Convenience,

00:02:21.219 --> 00:02:25.930
a sitcom he recently criticized, not only
for its premature cancelation, but also for

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:30.080
the way in which many of the Asian actors
were treated by the show's white creators.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.390
Liu also guest-starred as Taiwanese noodle
seller Willie in the 100th episode of ABC's

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.749
Fresh off the Boat, which aired in April 2019.

00:02:38.749 --> 00:02:43.459
The actor has himself underlined the need
for more Asian representation in the MCU,

00:02:43.459 --> 00:02:46.450
first tweeting such sentiments back in 2014.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:52.239
In 2019, he bought out a Toronto theater for
a screening of Awkwafina's film The Farewell,

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:55.409
citing the need for greater representation
for Asian actors.

00:02:55.409 --> 00:02:59.859
Going forward, it seems like the MCU couldn't
ask for a more passionate and devoted champion

00:02:59.859 --> 00:03:00.859
for the franchise.

00:03:01.889 --> 00:03:06.760
To many Western moviegoers, the name Tony
Leung won't be immediately familiar, but he's

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:10.970
one of the most high-profile and celebrated
actors in the Hong Kong film industry.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:15.040
Leung's career dates all the way back to the
'70s, and he's starred in everything from

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.999
rom-coms to thrillers to martial arts movies.

00:03:17.999 --> 00:03:22.950
During his long and storied career, Leung
has won a number of prestigious Hong Kong

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:27.579
Film Awards and earned Best Actor at the 2000
Cannes Film Festival for his leading role

00:03:27.579 --> 00:03:30.319
in Wong Kar-wai's In the Mood for Love.

00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:32.489
In short: he's a big deal.

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:36.849
For Shang-Chi, Leung has been cast as the
film's antagonist: the Mandarin.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:41.609
This, of course, is a subversion of the fake
Mandarin played by Ben Kingsley in Iron Man

00:03:41.609 --> 00:03:42.609
3.

00:03:42.609 --> 00:03:43.609
"It's just a role.

00:03:43.609 --> 00:03:46.909
The Mandarin, you see, it's not real."

00:03:46.909 --> 00:03:51.870
The 2014 short film Marvel One-Shot: All Hail
the King first revealed that there was indeed

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.219
a very real Mandarin operating from the shadows.

00:03:55.219 --> 00:03:58.989
According to the trailers for Shang-Chi, it
seems Leung's character is the leader of the

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:03.859
Ten Rings organization, the criminal organization
that debuted in the first Iron Man movie.

00:04:03.859 --> 00:04:07.900
In Shang-Chi, it appears that the Mandarin
has trained his son, Shang-Chi, to become

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:12.779
an assassin — and now he's ready for our
hero to take his place in the family business.

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:17.600
Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings
will find its titular hero out and about in

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.710
the normal world.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:23.030
Sure, he was trained as an assassin by his
villainous father, but Shang-Chi doesn't want

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.240
anything to do with his criminal group.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:29.310
Instead, he's spending his days in San Francisco,
living out a normal life and hanging out with

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:34.170
his BFF and co-worker Katy — who's played
by none other than Awkwafina.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:39.130
Awkwafina broke into the entertainment world
as a rap artist in 2014 with her debut album

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:45.280
Yellow Ranger, followed in 2018 by an EP entitled
In Fina We Trust.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.870
Not content to sit on her laurels, she turned
her eye to acting, making her major breakthrough

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:54.920
in 2018 with the one-two combo of Ocean's
8 and Crazy Rich Asians.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:58.910
The very next year found her starring in The
Farewell, a drama about a Chinese-American

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:03.070
family heading overseas to pay one last visit
to their dying matriarch.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:08.380
The movie also features Hong Kong action legend
Michelle Yeoh, who plays Jiang Nan, the hero's

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:15.460
ally and mentor, Fala Chen as Jiang Li, his
mother, and Meng'er Zhang as Xialing, Shang-Chi's

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.460
sister.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:22.230
Meanwhile, Ronny Chieng is playing Shang-Chi's
friend, Jon Jon, and Florian Munteanu will

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:25.000
appear as the intimidating Razor Fist.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:29.810
After much speculation and a blink-and-you'll-miss-it
trailer appearance, Doctor Strange actor Benedict

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:34.500
Wong confirmed that his character, Wong, will
also be featured in the movie.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.890
Not much else is known right now, but you
can bet your bottom dollar that a few more

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.960
familiar faces will show up before those credits
roll.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:46.690
As you might imagine, the Ten Rings themselves
are going to play a pretty big part in Shang-Chi's

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:47.690
plot.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:48.690
But what exactly are they?

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:52.720
Well, there are two interpretations to take
into account here, and it's looking like both

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.230
will be relevant for the movie's story.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:59.370
Longtime MCU fans doubtlessly know that the
Ten Rings is a terrorist organization that

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.350
kidnapped Tony Stark way back in Iron Man.

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:06.580
It's also revealed in Ant-Man that the group
is very interested in buying Darren Cross'

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.090
weaponized Yellow Jacket technology.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:13.230
They're sort-of featured in Iron Man 3 as
well, claiming responsibility for a number

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:15.340
of explosions across the U.S.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:19.770
Of course, it turns out the Ten Rings organization
has nothing to do with these events, and the

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:24.700
so-called Mandarin leading them is really
an alcoholic actor being manipulated by a

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.560
psychotic businessman.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:30.320
But now, it looks like we're getting the real
Ten Rings — and this appears to be a bunch

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.020
of people you really don't want to be messing
with.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:36.040
However, there's another meaning behind the
name "Ten Rings."

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:40.830
In the comics, the Ten Rings are magical pieces
of jewelry that imbue special powers to the

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:41.830
user.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:45.780
They're the Mandarin's primary weapons, and
each performs a different type of attack,

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:49.510
ranging from fire and ice beams to matter
and mind control.

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:53.440
The movie version of the rings are more like
bracelets worn on the user's arms, but their

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:56.910
powers appear to be similar to their comic
book counterparts.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:00.010
Expect them to play a pivotal role in Shang-Chi's
story.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:04.780
Long before the trailers for Shang-Chi hit
the internet, there were rumors that the Marvel

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:07.610
movie might also be a martial arts tournament
film.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:13.020
In fact, a few years ago, Murphy's Multiverse
claimed to have seen a casting call for "tournament

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.020
announcers."

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:17.620
Now that two trailers for the movie have been
released, it seems pretty clear that there

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:22.360
will indeed be some kind of tournament featured
in the movie — in which Shang-Chi will battle

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.330
his own sister, Xialing.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:29.200
This tourney is also the setting for a showdown
between two familiar MCU faces: the sorcerer

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:33.090
Wong and the Incredible Hulk villain known
as the Abomination.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:37.560
This kind of setting makes sense, of course,
as Destin Daniel Cretton has drawn influence

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:42.780
from a variety of martial arts films for Shang-Chi
— including the graceful wuxia stylings

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:47.050
of Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon and the
more frenetic pacing of Jackie Chan's action

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.050
flicks.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:51.480
Everyone knew that Shang-Chi was going to
be an action flick.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:57.389
After all, the original comic book character
was inspired by the legendary Bruce Lee.

00:07:57.389 --> 00:07:59.500
[Yelling]

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:04.810
However, judging by the trailers, it looks
like the movie might also be dipping its toe

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:07.240
into the fantasy genre, too.

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:11.750
One trailer, for example, sees Shang-Chi encountering
a gigantic dragon.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:16.200
Word has it that this massive beast is called
"the Great Protector," and will assist our

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.860
hero with its "benevolent power."

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:22.810
In addition, the movie's trailers have offered
a few glimpses of some huge lions, which could

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:27.460
be a nod to the Chinese guardian lions that
guard Imperial landmarks such as tombs and

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:28.460
palaces.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:33.450
On top of all that, a few leaked toys seem
to be indicating that a Dijiang might show

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.140
up somewhere in the film.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:39.950
These are furry, faceless creatures with wings
that, according to Chinese legend, are perpetually

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:42.380
confused and love to sing and dance.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:46.730
Could we be about to see the Marvel Cinematic
Universe's first ever twenty-minute karaoke

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:48.200
dance sequence?

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.230
Here's hoping.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.240
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.510
Plus, even more Looper videos about the MCU
are coming soon.

